MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Step Back and Goin' Home feel like natural follow-ups to Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels because blues and expressive guitar playing are what appeal to me right now.",
    "Hypnotic Eye is especially compelling after You Should Be So Lucky because the Tom Petty connection gives me a specific reason to explore it next."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Loved Me Back to Life and Wallflower do not offer the guitar-driven blues-rock feel I am seeking, even though they also feature established performers.",
    "Morning Phase feels too quiet for my current mood, and Chicago's Now does not draw me in as strongly as the blues-oriented choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Familiar, established performers alone are not enough to make an album relevant to me; the sound and connection to my recent listening matter more.",
    "My interaction with Blown Away suggests some country interest, but it does not mean country is what I want to choose on this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent interaction, You Should Be So Lucky, makes the connection to Hypnotic Eye particularly meaningful today.",
    "I choose very few albums, so an appealing blues-rock sound may still not be enough: the Black Crowes live album interests me, but feels less compelling today than Step Back or Hypnotic Eye."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understand my interest in blues and established rock performers, but sometimes mistake broad familiarity for the specific sound and musical connections that motivate me to choose."
}
